\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  Rupiah Ends Higher On Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 294 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 2005\par 12:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2005, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah extended its recovery by another 1.2% Wednesday as Bank Indonesia reportedly sold dollars and sent auditors to foreign banks' dealing rooms in Jakarta to deter \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at IDR9,573, down from its close Tuesday at IDR9,688. The rupiah had risen 0.6% Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said that the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively unloaded dollars via brokers to prop up the rupiah. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  couldn't be reached for comment, but its officials have said recently that the bank would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the rupiah when necessary.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said that Bank Indonesia also dispatched its auditors to look at foreign banks' transaction activity.  \par \par \uc2 'Suddenly, we saw a dollar selloff today from foreign banks, who likely unloaded their dollar long positions after central banks sent their auditors to those banks,' a dealer with a local bank said.  \par \par \uc2 Foreign banks are the main players in Jakarta's interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said that dollar demand from local companies also abated as they chose to wait on the sidelines, likely hoping to buy the greenback at lower levels.  \par \par \uc2 The market welcomed President Susilo Bambang Yudhoyono's call earlier Wednesday for his ministers to coordinate closely with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost the rupiah's value, which recently fell to over-three-year lows.  \par \par \uc2 'It shows that the president is in charge on this (rupiah weakness) problem,' a dealer with a local bank said.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expect the dollar to continue sliding Thursday. They, however, forecast a wide IDR9,500-IDR9,750 range as the market remains unstable. -By I Made Sentana; Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -0-  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020050427e14r008ev\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
