\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Indonesia c.bank soaks up cash to help rupiah.  \b0\par\par\uc2 481 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 2005\par 13:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, April 26 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched a three-day \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  tool on Tuesday and said it could raise interest rates in an effort to soak up excess rupiah in the banking system as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to three-year lows.  \par \par \uc2 The new deposit facility, which Bank Indonesia called a fine tuning instrument, offered banks a rate of 3.625 percent. It attracted 1.69 trillion rupiah ($174.7 million) from the market.  \par \par \uc2 "The auction has helped push up rates. The overnight rate is now being offered at above four percent. It was below that before the announcement," a bank dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is under pressure to support the battered rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which hit a three-year low of 9,800 per dollar on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Governor Burhanuddin Abdullah said on Tuesday the central banks was studying the possibility of raising the reserve requirements for commercial banks to help the rupiah.  \par \par \uc2 He also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would lift the interest rates on its short-term debt certificates.  \par \par \uc2 "We plan to absorb liquidity by raising interest rates, possibly by 15-20 basis points," he told reporters, without giving a specific timeframe.  \par \par \uc2 The rupiah has weakened on expectations that rising world oil prices will lead to increased demand for dollars to pay for oil imports. The dollar buying leads to excess rupiah in the money market, which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trying to absorb to stop the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  falling and counter inflation risks.  \par \par \uc2 Worries over the rupiah hurt sentiment at an auction of two-year bonds on Tuesday, the proceeds of which would be used to help finance budget deficit.  \par \par \uc2 The government raised a targeted three trillion rupiah from the monthly auction at an average yield of 9.77 percent, well above a forecast of 9.54 percent from a Reuters survey.  \par \par \uc2 A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official told Reuters that under the new three day facility banks would deposit money at Bank Indonesia. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not exchange any assets for the cash, so it was not a repurchase agreement or an issue of debt paper, the official said.  \par \par \uc2 The three-day facility adds to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's relatively limited number of tools to absorb liquidity. They include a seven-day \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  facility, plus one-month and three-month \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  certificates (SBIs).  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has used its seven-day \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  facility daily of late, and offer its three-day instrument only when it is deemed necessary.  \par \par \uc2 The interest rate on the three-day facility may vary regularly, unlike the seven-day rate which is changed only occasionally, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the seven-day rate by 25 basis points to 7.25 percent earlier this month, after annual inflation hit a 27-month high of 8.8 percent in March.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050426e14q008f2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\