\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesia Rupiah Ends Up On  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Moves  \b0\par\par\uc2 435 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 2005\par 12:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesia rupiah recovered from volatile trading Tuesday after Bank Indonesia unloaded U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market and stated plans to stop the dollar's rally, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at IDR9,688, down from its close Monday at IDR9,750. But the greenback touched a fresh three-year high of IDR9,810 earlier Tuesday as panic-stricken local companies continue to hedge offshore obligations.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers estimated that Bank Indonesia sold around $150 million in the spot market, which helped the rupiah recover.  \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia's Governor Burhanuddin Abdullah said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will take a raft of measures to support the rupiah, including raising its benchmark Sertifikat Bank Indonesia, or SBI, interest rate by 15 to 20 basis points. The rate on the one-month SBI now stands at 7.7%. The rupiah's decline has also prompted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to consider rolling out newer, more sophisticated money-market management tools, including a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap instrument, to reduce U.S.-dollar buying by state-owned companies, Bank Indonesia Senior Deputy Governor Miranda Gultom said. She didn't provide a timetable for such a move.  \par \par \uc2 The bank's plan includes a temporary decrease in commercial banks' net open position to 20% of equity capital from 30%, effective immediately. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also considering increasing banks' reserve requirement ratios as an added measure to absorb excess liquidity in the financial system. Commercial banks currently must maintain a minimum reserve ratio of 5%.  \par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  will also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market via forward transactions to defend the value of the rupiah against the U.S. dollar, Burhanuddin said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will take a much more proactive stance against state-owned firms whose dollar purchases have been linked to the decline in the value of the rupiah against the U.S. dollar, the governor indicated.  \par \par \uc2 Burhanuddin was quoted Tuesday by Bisnis Indonesia as naming state-run oil company Pertamina and electricity company Perusahaan Listrik Negara as examples of state-owned firms currently securing large quantities of U.S. dollars to pay foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -denominated bills that come due up to six months in the future.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said that demand for the dollar may resurface Wednesday as the end of the month is drawing nearer. They expect the dollar to trade between IDR9,650 and IDR9,750, with Bank Indonesia expected to enter the market again.  \par \par \uc2 -By I Made Sentana; Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by E. Beiser [ 26-04-05 1006GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1159 1848  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050426e14q000io\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
