\par\par \b \uc2 Bk Indonesia Chief: Rate Hike Planned To Defend Rupiah  \b0\par\par\uc2 595 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 2005\par 08:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Bank Indonesia Governor Burhanuddin Abdullah said Tuesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will raise its benchmark Sertifikat Bank Indonesia, or SBI, interest rate by 15 to 20 basis points to defend the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  following a recent slide in its value against the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The planned increase in the SBI rate will help the rupiah by draining excess liquidity out of the system, Burhanuddin told reporters, without elaborating on a timetable for the rate hike.  \par \par \uc2 The next auction of SBI notes, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's money market papers, is scheduled for next Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The rate on the one-month SBI stands at 7.7%. [ 26-04-05 0711GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  plan spurred a rebound in the value of the rupiah against the U.S. dollar to IDR9,678 at 0728 GMT from a more than three-year low of IDR9,810 at 0435 GMT, dealers told Dow Jones Newswires.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at IDR9,750 Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers have blamed the slide in the value of the rupiah against the dollar on local firms' purchased of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hedge offshore obligations.  \par \par \uc2 A weaker rupiah threatens the financial performance of local firms which have substantial dollar debt, which in turn could hurt the nation's economy. The Indonesian government and private companies have around $130 billion in foreign debt.  \par \par \uc2 The rupiah's fall has also prompted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to consider rolling out newer, more sophisticated money market management tools, including a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap instrument, to reduce U.S.-dollar buying by state-owned companies, Bank Indonesia's Senior Deputy Governor Miranda Gultom said. He didn't provide a timetable for such a move.  \par \par \uc2 Governor Burhanuddin indicated that the planned interest rate increase is justified to boost the value of the rupiah against the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling dollars Tuesday morning to stem the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide.  \par \par \uc2 "At a 9,600-level effective exchange rate, the rupiah is undervalued by 9% against the U.S. dollar," Burhanuddin said.  \par \par \uc2 He said the pending rate hike is part of a four-point \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  plan to stabilize the rupiah's value.  \par \par \uc2 That plan includes a temporary decrease in commercial banks' net open position to 20% of equity capital from 30%, effective immediately. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also considering increasing banks' reserve requirement ratios as an added measure to absorb excess liquidity in the financial system. Commercial banks currently must maintain a minimum reserve ratio of 5%.  \par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  will also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market via forward transactions to defend the value of the rupiah against the U.S. dollar, Burhanuddin said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will take a much more proactive stance against state-owned firms whose dollar purchases have been linked to the decline in the value of the rupiah against the U.S. dollar, the governor indicated.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has reached an agreement with the government to monitor dollar purchases of up to $150 million daily by state-owned petroleum firm Pertamina (PTM.YY), Burhanuddin said, without giving further details.  \par \par \uc2 A report in the Bisnis Indonesia daily on Tuesday, citing Burhanuddin, named Pertamina and electricity company PT Perusahaan Listrik Negara as examples of state-owned firms currently securing large quantities of U.S. dollars to pay foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -denominated bills that come due up to six months in the future.  \par \par \uc2 -By Linda Silaen and Phelim Kyne, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21-39831277; dj.jakarta@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Lena Lee [ 26-04-05 0855GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050426e14q0008u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
