\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Indonesia Rupiah Ends Flat; Exporters Sell Dollars  \b0\par\par\uc2 213 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 April 2005\par 12:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2005, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah closed steady Tuesday as exporters unloaded dollars, helping to offset demand from local importers, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at IDR9,575, unchanged from its close Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said exporters sold the dollar to take advantage of its recent gains against the rupiah.  \par \par \uc2 'Exporters were probably happy with the rupiah's current levels to exchange their dollars to local money,' a dealer with a foreign bank said.  \par \par \uc2 Importers - notably the oil company Pertamina - however, continued to collect greenbacks to settle their trade bills, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not thought to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market Tuesday, probably because the rupiah was stable.  \par \par \uc2 The nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said recently it would unload the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reduce volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 The pressure on the rupiah also abated slightly as capital outflows from the Indonesian stock market seemed to stop, dealers said. The Jakarta Stock Exchange's main index rose 0.2% Tuesday, recovering from a 3.3% loss Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expect the dollar to trade between IDR9,550 and IDR9,590 Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 -By I Made Sentana; Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Paul Baylis  \par \par \uc2 -0-  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020050419e14j007hl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict