\par\par \b \uc2 PRESS DIGEST-Indonesian Business News - April 6.  \b0\par\par\uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 2005\par 03:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 Following are the leading stories in the main Indonesian newspapers on April 6. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy. Telephone: Editorial, (6221) 384-6364. Fax: (6221) 344-8404 or Help Desk, +803 061 2124 (toll free).  \par \par \uc2 - - - -  \par \par \uc2 BISNIS \b \highlight22\uc2 INDONESIA\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 - BANK \b \highlight22\uc2 INDONESIA\b0 \highlight\uc2  WILL KEEP \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENING\b0 \highlight\uc2  AS NEEDED  \par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to avoid sharp fluctuation in the rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  , a deputy governor of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 - INDOSAT TO GO AHEAD WITH BOND ISSUE PLANS  \par \par \uc2 PT Indosat Tbk (ISAT.JK), indonesia's second largest telecommunications company, will go ahead with its plan to issue around $300-$400 million in rupiah and dollar bonds, its finance director said.  \par \par \uc2 - - - -  \par \par \uc2 KOMPAS  \par \par \uc2 - BANKS WANT SBI RATES TO INCREASE BY 6-11 BASIS POINTS  \par \par \uc2 Most Indonesian banks want SBI rates to rise by 6-11 basis points at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  auction on Wednesday, some bank directors said. Bank Indonesia said it will absorb a total of 74 trillion rupiah ($7.83 billion) from the auction.  \par \par \uc2 - - - -  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA POST  \par \par \uc2 - SUSILO HOPES FOR MORE AUSTRALIAN INVESTMENT  \par \par \uc2 President Susilo Bambang Yudhoyono concluded his trip to Australia by meeting local business leaders in the country in an attemp to lure more Australian investment to Indonesia.  \par \par \uc2 - JAKARTA VOWS TO BOOST OIL OUTPUT BY 300,000 BPD  \par \par \uc2 The Indonesian government reiterated its pledge on Tuesday to boost the country's oil output by 300,000 barrels per day by 2008-2009 to meet increasing demand in the domestic market, the energy minister said.  \par \par \uc2 ($1=9,445 rupiah)  \par \par \uc2 - - - -  \par \par \uc2 Looking for more information from local sources? For details, please call your local help desk .   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050406e1460010e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
