\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Indonesia raises key rate on inflation worries.  \b0\par\par\uc2 524 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 April 2005\par 13:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, April 4 (Reuters) - Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , worried by rising inflation, on Monday raised a key interest rate by a quarter percentage point and said it was ready to act again.  \par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  increased its benchmark seven-day \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate to 7.25 percent on Monday, the first change since it was introduced in June 2004. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  previously used an overnight rate, which it stopped using in January.  \par \par \uc2 Jakarta stocks shrugged off the largely expected rate rise, with analysts seeing limited impact on corporate earnings, while the rupiah and local bonds continued their downtrends.  \par \par \uc2 "We are monitoring market conditions. We will again raise it if needed," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy governor Maulana Ibrahim told reporters at an economic seminar in the central Java town of Yogyakarta.  \par \par \uc2 Annual inflation climbed to 8.8 percent in March, the highest rate in more than two years, according to data on Friday. A sharp increase in fuel prices was the main culprit.  \par \par \uc2 The 7-day \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, also known as the Fasbi, is used by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to manage the amount of funds in the money market.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the rate rise was likely to be followed by bigger rate increases on benchmark one-month and three-month \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  paper (SBI), and they expected SBI rates to hover at around 8.0 to 8.5 percent at most by year end.  \par \par \uc2 The rate on one-month SBIs has crept higher at auctions to 7.44 percent in March from 7.40 percent in October. Three-month SBIs have held at around 7.3 percent since October.  \par \par \uc2 LIMITED IMPACT  \par \par \uc2 Monday's rate hike "is not going to hit corporate earnings. Debt-to-equity ratio of Indonesian corporates is quite low, they are not highly indebted," said a senior research analyst at a large foreign fund management firm in Jakarta.  \par \par \uc2 He said the debt ratio at some firms was around 30 percent following a restructuring drive after the Asian financial crisis of 1997/1998.  \par \par \uc2 Jakarta stocks did not seem too perturbed by the rate rise, ending 0.47 percent higher at 1,100.20 points on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 However, the rate rise did not support the rupiah much. It lost a quarter percent to 9,480 against the dollar. The rupiah is the second-worst-performing Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year after the yen, partly due to domestic inflationary pressures.  \par \par \uc2 Government bond prices weakened slightly, extending a recent downward trend, with the rate rise further dampening sentiment already hurt by the spike in inflation, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 Total outstanding Fasbi facilities currently stand at 74 trillion rupiah ($7.8 billion), against a more normal figure of 5-10 trillion rupiah.  \par \par \uc2 The Fasbi amount has jumped sharply as investors took advantage of the facility last week when SBIs matured and there was no auction of new SBI paper, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said.  \par \par \uc2 But the amount will likely return to its normal level after an SBI auction on Wednesday, he said.  \par \par \uc2 Total outstanding SBIs, widely held by investors, particularly commercial banks, stand at around 57 trillion rupiah. ($1=9,480 rupiah).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050404e144003ml\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\