\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesia Rupiah Ends Down;Suspected Dlr Sales By Ctrl Bk  \b0\par\par\uc2 290 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 10:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah ended lower Thursday against the dollar, with dealers saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the local unit's slide.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at IDR9,418, up from its close of IDR9,390 Wednesday, as a delay in a $1 billion sovereign bond issue and in the government's sale of a local bank stake hurt sentiment on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Yusuf Anwar confirmed earlier reports that the government has delayed the offering until global bond markets calm.  \par \par \uc2 The government also shelved the sale of a 5% stake in Bank Central Asia late Wednesday after it failed to get good bids. It had expected to raise around $250 million from the sale.  \par \par \uc2 "The two delays mean there will be no capital inflows soon," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier in the day. Although its dollar sales were well absorbed, the selling still managed to pull the U.S. unit off an intraday high of IDR9,430.  \par \par \uc2 Officials at Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to confirm the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite dealers saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  routinely sells dollars if the rupiah is under selling pressure.  \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia Governor Burhanuddin Abdullah said Tuesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue to sell dollars if necessary as the exchange rate is moving away from its target range of IDR8,800 to IDR9,200 this year.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expect the dollar to trade between IDR9,390 and IDR9,420 Monday.  \par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will be closed Friday for the Easter holiday.  \par \par \uc2 -By I Made Sentana; Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Lena Lee [ 24-03-05 0921GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1159 1848  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050324e13o000di\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
