\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesia Rupiah Ends Up As Dlr Loses Gains Vs Yen  \b0\par\par\uc2 243 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 10:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah ended slightly higher Wednesday as dealers locked in profits against the dollar after the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to keep overnight gains on the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at IDR9,390, down slightly from its close Tuesday at IDR9,395.  \par \par \uc2 The greenback touched an earlier high of IDR9,425 in reaction to a further 25 basis point hike in U.S. interest rates overnight, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Against the Japanese yen, the dollar was traded at Y105.47 at 0850 GMT, down from 105.57-59 at 2150 GMT Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 "Market participants took profit as the market seemed to have been caught long (on dollars)," a dealer with a foreign bank said.  \par \par \uc2 Local exporters were also heard to be selling the dollar in the market, which helped the rupiah.  \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia was suspected of selling dollars via state banks. Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's governor said Tuesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  that day and would continue to do so in the future as necessary. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually doesn't confirm specific \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expect the dollar to trade between IDR9,370 and IDR9,400 Thursday, with the dollar-yen movement expected to continue providing guidance to the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 -By I Made Sentana; Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com  \par \par \