\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  c.bank says  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to help rupiah.   \b0\par\par\uc2 124 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 10:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, March 22 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prop up the weakening rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Burhanuddin Abdullah said on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been done. We will keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it is needed," Abdullah told reporters. He said the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week and again on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 The rupiah was trading at 9,370/9,400 to the dollar, significantly weaker that the government's forecast average rate for this year of 8,600 rupiah.   \par \par \uc2 The 14-days moving average for the unit stood at 9,351 to the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Many traders have blamed oil purchases by state-owned company Pertamina for the weaker rupiah.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050322e13m0079f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
