\par\par \b \uc2 Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2 : To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  To Help Rupiah If Needed  \b0\par\par\uc2 136 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 2004\par 07:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Thursday it was ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the rupiah after a massive bomb killed at least three people outside the Australian embassy in Jakarta.  \par \par \uc2 "We are going to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if necessary," Aslim Tadjuddin, a deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, told Dow Jones Newswires. But he declined to say whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had already been active Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The rupiah weakness is likely only temporary, he said.  \par \par \uc2 Still, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has fallen heavily following the blast. Around 0513 GMT, the dollar was trading at IDR9,375, up from IDR9,288 before the bombing.  \par \par \uc2 -By Edhi Pranasidhi, Dow Jones Newswires; 6221 3983 1277; edhi.pranasidhi@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Mary de Wet [ 09-09-04 0519GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040909e0990007m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
