\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesia Rupiah Ends At 8-Wk Low On Corporate Dlr Demand  \b0\par\par\uc2 217 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 2004\par 11:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah closed at an eight-week low Friday on rising dollar demand from local companies to pay offshore obligations at the end of the month.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at 9,320 rupiah, up from its close of IDR9,290 Thursday and its highest closing level since June 30, when it ended at IDR9,395.  \par \par \uc2 A correction in the dollar against most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, slowed down its rise versus the rupiah, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "Most offshore players sold the dollar on rises," said a dealer with a foreign bank.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said there was no sign of Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market Friday to help the rupiah. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected of selling the greenback Thursday via state banks.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expect the dollar to trade in a higher range Monday between IDR9,290 and IDR9,350 as more local companies are likely to buy dollars for month-end debt repayments.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers also expect local companies to accumulate dollars in the near term as the political temperature rises ahead of the presidential runoff Sept. 20.  \par \par \uc2 -By I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; 6221-3983-1277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Shishir Mudgil [ 27-08-04 0933GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1159 1848  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040827e08r000gu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
