\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Small losses after U.S. rate rise.  \b0\par\par\uc2 754 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 2004\par 10:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Aug 11 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  suffered\par modest losses on Wednesday after the United States raised\par rates, although they lagged the yen and benefited from the\par market's apparent unwillingness to buy the U.S. dollar\par aggressively.\par     Traders said recent weakness in U.S. economic data,\par particularly jobs, continued to weigh on the dollar. Regionals\par also found support in the view that Asian authorities would\par defend their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to ease the pressure from oil prices.\par     As expected, the U.S. Fed raised rates by 25 basis points\par to 1.5 percent on Tuesday, following a similar quarter point\par rise on June 30. The Fed said the economy had been hit by\par higher energy costs but was poised for faster growth.\par     Crude oil prices        hit fresh highs over $45 a barrel\par on Tuesday, complicating the outlook for global growth and\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "To the extent that global conditions for growth\par deteriorate via higher oil prices, that should be bearish\par dollar," said Ray Farris, markets strategist with CSFB in\par Singapore.\par     But higher oil prices would also be a negative factor for\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the heavy oil-importing Asian economies, the\par only difference being that authorities in Asia often used\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as policy tools, he said.\par     "Higher oil prices mean higher inflation in a region that\par already has higher inflation, so it is difficult to allow\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to depreciate and import further inflation."\par  \par     The Japanese yen        fell more than 0.6 percent from\par Tuesday's levels and was quoted near 111.30/40 a dollar.\par     Barring the usually volatile Indonesian rupiah, most Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had minimal losses.\par     The rupiah        was back at Monday's one-month lows near\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 9,270 a dollar despite a suspicion the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to defend the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Tuesday and Bank  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's stating it would keep domestic cash conditions  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 tight.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The Thai baht        fell to 41.50, testing an 11-month low\par hit late in July.\par     The Singapore dollar        erased gains it made on Tuesday\par on the back of unexpectedly strong GDP data. It fell over a\par quarter of a percent to 1.7160/70 a dollar.\par     The Korean won                   and Taiwan dollar\par fell slightly, but found support in rallying stock markets and\par the Fed's optimism on the economy.\par     "If the global outlook for growth begins to deteriorate, it\par will be unpalatable for Asia to appreciate \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and it\par will be unpalatable to increase interest rates," Farris said.\par     That meant Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would not be allowed to\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 depreciate, nor would any appreciation that hurt export  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 competitiveness be tolerated until the growth outlook improved,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Farris said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BUY VOLATILITY  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Merrill Lynch strategist Vincent Low said in a note the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 stability in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would not be sustained and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 markets should brace for volatility.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Either U.S. dollar-Asia eventually breaks lower as policy is  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 tightened or breaks higher as investors take a view that policy  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 is behind the curve and rising inflation translates to capital  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 outflows and weakening \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," Low said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There was the danger of emerging Asia mimicking the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese yen's moves against the U.S. dollar, and it was a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 mistake for non-Japan Asia to import the policy of the country  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 with the lowest inflation, he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With the risk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moving out of their ranges and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 quite sharply in either direction, investors could hedge  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 themselves by buying cheap volatility, he said. Implied  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 volatility on one-year Korean won is around 7.5  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 percent, the lowest since February 2003.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Owning volatility is one way to express this view without  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 taking a directional bet on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," Low said.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0805 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Cur