\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesian Rupiah Ends Steady, Tracking USD/JPY Movement  \b0\par\par\uc2 192 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 2004\par 11:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah ended steady against the dollar Thursday after the U.S. unit gave up its gains against the yen, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at 9,405 rupiah, virtually unchanged from its close Wednesday at IDR9,400.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar rose to an intraday high of IDR9,430 early in the day as local companies bought the U.S. unit following its rise against the yen to above Y110.  \par \par \uc2 However, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  retreated against the yen in late Asian trading, spurring dollar-selling against the rupiah.  \par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't heard \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market Thursday, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely doesn't see any need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as long as the dollar is still below IDR9,425," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expect the dollar-rupiah to continue tracking the dollar-yen movement Friday. However, they believe demand from local companies will likely prevent the dollar from falling below IDR9,380.  \par \par \uc2 -By I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; 6221-3983-1277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Shishir Mudgil [ 17-06-04 0914GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1159 1848  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040617e06h000d5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
