\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesian Rupiah Ends Lower; Corp Dlr Demand Resurfaces  \b0\par\par\uc2 303 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 2004\par 11:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah ended lower Thursday as local companies bought the dollar following its rise against the yen, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar's rebound against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dashed hopes of a further dollar slide against the rupiah in the short run, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at 9,385 rupiah, up from its close at IDR9,285 Wednesday. The dollar rose to an intraday high of IDR9,420 after the dollar rebounded above Y110 in early Asian trading. But it failed to maintain the gain against the yen, and that also dragged it from its high against the rupiah.  \par \par \uc2 Local companies in the past three days were mostly absent from the market, waiting to buy the U.S. unit at lower levels to hedge foreign debt payments on concerns over political fighting ahead of next month's presidential election.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said foreign players also bought back the dollar to cover their dollar-short positions.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't spotted in the market to help the rupiah Thursday, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "I didn't hear any talk of Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been active recently in the market to defend the rupiah. But it said Wednesday that the rupiah's recent weakness to a 26-month low isn't yet expected to have significant negative impact on the economy.  \par \par \uc2 Some analysts said the rupiah weakness may help the country's struggling exports.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said corporate dollar demand will continue to persist Friday, which will likely push the greenback as high as IDR9,425, with support predicted at IDR9,350.  \par \par \uc2 -By I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Mary de Wet [ 10-06-04 0938GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1159 1848  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040610e06a000f3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
