\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesian Rupiah Ends Steady On Suspected Ctrl Bk Action  \b0\par\par\uc2 215 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 2004\par 11:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah ended steady in thin trading Wednesday as suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offset demand for the dollar, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at 9,285 rupiah, little changed from its close Tuesday at IDR9,280.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said that local companies still bought dollars to hedge offshore loans on lingering concerns over political fighting ahead of next month presidential election.  \par \par \uc2 Foreign market players also bought back the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cover their dollar-short positions built in the past two days, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, was believed to have sold dollars via state banks. The nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly said it would continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help the rupiah.  \par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Wednesday that the rupiah recent weakness hasn't yet had significant negative impact of the Indonesian economy and it remains optimistic that the country could achieve close to 5% economic growth this year.  \par \par \uc2 Some analysts said the rupiah's fall could benefit Indonesian exports.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expect the dollar to trade between IDR8,260 and IDR9,300 Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 -By I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; 6221-3983-1277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Shishir Mudgil [ 09-06-04 0920GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1159 1848  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI00000