\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesian Rupiah Ends Sharply Lower As Yen Slumps Vs Dlr  \b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Mai 2004\par 11:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah ended sharply lower Monday as the dollar surged against the yen on expectations for an early interest rate hike in the U.S., dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar finished at 8,950 rupiah, its highest close since March 24. It ended at IDR8,735 Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said reports that Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to help the rupiah failed to lift the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia Deputy Governor Aslim Tadjudin warned Monday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, if needed, to curb excessive volatility.  \par \par \uc2 "Bank Indonesia is ready to do something," he told reporters when asked if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Aslim attributed the rupiah's weakness partly to the dollar's gains versus other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on expectations the U.S. economy is gathering pace.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. employment data issued Friday showed 288,000 jobs were created in April, outstripping market expectations for 150,000 new jobs. The stronger-than-expected data fueled expectations that Federal Reserve policy-makers will start raising rates early this summer.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said a recent fall in the Indonesian equity market has also damped rupiah sentiment.  \par \par \uc2 On Monday, the Jakarta Stock Exchange's main index slipped 4.9% to 707.218 points, down for the eight consecutive session.  \par \par \uc2 Some analysts predicted the dollar may rise to around IDR9,000 on political concerns in the run-up to the presidential elections in July.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said they expect the dollar to retain its upside bias against the rupiah Tuesday, and that it will likely continue to track its performance against the yen.  \par \par \uc2 -By Jakarta Bureau, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; djn.jakarta@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Ryan Woo [ 10-05-04 0929GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1159 1848  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040510e05a000gt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
