\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesian Rupiah Ends Down Tracking Dlr's Surge Vs Yen  \b0\par\par\uc2 320 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 April 2004\par 11:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah closed lower Wednesday, tracking the dollar's surge against the yen in Asia, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at 8,650 rupiah, up from its close of IDR8,615 Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to slow down the dollar's rise, which was triggered by its surge to above Y109 against the Japanese yen in late Asian trading.  \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia usually sells the dollar in the spot market to help the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It has said that it expects the dollar to trade between IDR8,200 and IDR8,700 in the second quarter of the year. Dealers said the market takes this level as a virtual trading band tolerated by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the market's reaction to Tuesday's nomination of Gen. Wiranto by the Golongan Karya party, or Golkar, as its presidential candidate for the July 5 election was muted.  \par \par \uc2 The market still largely predicts former security minister Susilo Bambang Yudhoyono, who has named ex-social welfare minister Yusuf Kalla as his running mate, to take over at the helm.  \par \par \uc2 Still, Golkar which is considered the best organized political group with the most money, will push hard to elect him.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say foreign investors will most likely react negatively to a Wiranto victory as the U.N. prosecutors in East Timor have indicted him for human rights abuses.  \par \par \uc2 Indonesia could face international isolation and international donors may become reluctant to support the country if Wiranto becomes president, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 "The rupiah will be under pressure if the market sees signs of a Wiranto victory," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expect the dollar to trade between IDR8,620 and IDR8,675 Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 -By I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Shishir Mudgil [ 21-04-04 0940GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1159 1848  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040421e04l000hc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
