\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesian Rupiah Ends Up; Suspected Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 265 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 April 2004\par 11:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah closed slightly higher against the dollar Friday on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar finished at 8,620 rupiah, down from its close Thursday at IDR8,635.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said Bank Indonesia was suspected of selling dollars via state banks to help the rupiah, which came under pressure recently as the dollar surged against its major rivals.  \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia has said it would sell dollars if necessary to defend the rupiah. It doesn't comment on specific \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategies, however.  \par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's deputy governor Aslim Tadjudin Friday downplayed the rupiah's recent weakness, saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall against the dollar is "temporary" and is partly due to a weakening in other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "The rupiah's weakness is temporary and not worrying," Aslim told reporters. He added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the rupiah is under pressure.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said foreign banks here sold dollars as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems to have lost some steam for now against the yen. Still, it remains unclear if the U.S. unit is poised for a sharp correction lower.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the market ignored domestic politics, at least for now, as the political situation in Indonesia appears to have entered a lull following last week's parliamentary elections.  \par \par \uc2 They expect the dollar to trade between IDR8,600 and IDR8,650 Monday.  \par \par \uc2 -By I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Ryan Woo [ 16-04-04 0917GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1159 1848  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040416e04g000ds\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
