\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesian Rupiah Ends Dn At 8-Mo Low On Dlr Surge Vs Yen  \b0\par\par\uc2 237 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 10:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah slid to an eight-month closing low Friday as foreign market participants bought the dollar following its surge against the yen.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at 8,590 rupiah, up from Thursday's close of IDR8,545. It last closed at IDR8,590 on July 24, 2003.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was trading at Y111.27 in late afternoon Friday, up from Y110.60 in Tokyo late Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 However, the dollar's rise against the rupiah may have been curbed by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dealers said Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  allegedly sold the dollar through state banks to keep the U.S. unit below IDR8,600.  \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia officials have previously said they were comfortable with the dollar between IDR8,200 and IDR8,600.  \par \par \uc2 "Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's alleged \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  managed to keep the dollar below IDR8,600, but demand from local companies continued to support it," said a dealer with a European bank in Jakarta.  \par \par \uc2 Local companies, saddled with $60 billion in total offshore borrowings, need the dollar to pay maturing debts.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the dollar may try to test IDR8,600 Monday as the greenback is expected to maintain its strength against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 -By I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Mary de Wet [ 05-03-04 0931GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1159 1848  \par \par \uc2 Dokumen