\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesian Rupiah Ends Higher After Global Bond Issue  \b0\par\par\uc2 183 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 10:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah closed higher Thursday after the country successfully launched $1 billion in global bonds.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at 8,545 rupiah, down from its close Wednesday at IDR8,560.  \par \par \uc2 The warm response this week to Indonesia's first global bond since the 1997-98 Asian crisis helped push the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher. The bond, which priced Wednesday in New York, received $4 billion in orders, signaling renewed confidence in \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed Thursday it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday to support the rupiah, which had fallen to four-month lows this week. The bank said it would continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when necessary, which added to positive sentiment toward the rupiah.  \par \par \uc2 The rupiah has been under pressure due to the dollar's strength against the yen and other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The dollar is expected to trade between IDR8,530 and IDR8,570 Friday, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 -By Tom Wright, Dow Jones Newswires; 6221 3983 1277; tom.wright@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Mary de Wet [ 04-03-04 0938GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1159 1848  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040304e034000bx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
