\par\par \b \uc2 Jakarta stocks may rise on speaker court ruling.   \b0\par\par\uc2 386 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 2004\par 03:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Feb 13 (Reuters) - Indonesian shares may rise on Friday after a ruling was issued in a high-profile graft case, ending uncertainty, and as fears over possible wide-spread unrest from the issue appeared unjustified.   \par \par \uc2 "We see the market testing 772 levels today. Yesterday the markets were hesitant while waiting for the Supreme Court ruling. Now I think the market could be positive," said Fitri Murniawati, an analyst at BNI Securities.   \par \par \uc2 After the market closed on Thursday the Supreme Court overturned a graft conviction of parliament speaker Akbar Tandjung, keeping him in place as a political powerhouse and potential presidential candidate.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts had said investors were concerned protesters outside the court building would spark wide-scale violence following the ruling, but that failed to materialise.   \par \par \uc2 Another supporting factor for the market would be cuts in Indonesia's interest rates this week.   \par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  reduced its overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate on Thursday by 25 basis points to 7.50 percent after the benchmark rate, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's one month certificate, fell by 11 basis points to 7.66 percent at Wednesday's auction.   \par \par \uc2 "The market had not priced in the interest rate decline, I think that factor could come into play today," Murniawati added.   \par \par \uc2 Several analysts said the cut would have a positive impact on banking shares.   \par \par \uc2 Shares of PT Indonesian Satellite Corp Tbk (ISAT.JK), the country's second largest telecommunication firm, may extend gains this session as analysts said the fair valuation of the stock was around 20,000 rupiah ($2.38) each, following various positive news items on the company.   \par \par \uc2 Indosat has posted a gain of almost 20 percent since announcing its plan for a stock split at a ratio of one to five earlier this month. But some dealers said investors might be tempted to lock in their gains.   \par \par \uc2 MARKET LEVELS   \par \par \uc2 The Jakarta Composite Index finished down 0.48 percent at 766.083 points on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 In New York, markets were down with the Dow Jones Industrial Average off 0.41 percent to 10,694.07 points and the Nasdaq Composite falling 0.77 percent to 2,073.61 points.   \par \par \uc2 The rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was being quoted at 8,415/8,420 to the dollar early on Friday, slightly lower than late Thursday's level.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040213e02d000cn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
