\par\par \b \uc2 Jakarta stocks may rise on rate cuts, bank shares.    \b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Februar 2004\par 03:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Feb 12 (Reuters) - Jakarta stocks may trade higher on Thursday following a series of cuts in the country's interest rates, which some analysts said could positively affect the banking sector.    \par \par \uc2 Gains in the Tokyo market and some other bourses in the region could also help sentiment.    \par \par \uc2 "The banking sector will be positive today, although the increase would not be solely due to the rate cuts, but also because of the divestment news," said Arwani Pranadjaya, technical analysts at Mandiri Sekuritas.    \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cut its rupiah overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, also known as FASBI, to 7.50 percent from 7.75 percent after a steeper-than-expected decrease on the rate of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's one-month certificate to 7.66 percent a day earlier.    \par \par \uc2 An Indonesian parliamentary commission agreed on Wednesday to the sale of a 71 percent stake of mid-size PT Bank Permata Tbk (BNLI.JK), valued around $730 million, and minority holdings in four other banks.    \par \par \uc2 Permata shares rose 12.5 percent following the news but Pranadjaya doubted the share could book further gains in the short run.    \par \par \uc2 The share price of PT Bank Danamon Tbk (BDMN.JK), the country's fifth largest, are expected to rise as the bank plans to announce what are expected to be good 2003 financial results later this month.    \par \par \uc2 A Reuters estimate produced an average of around 1.3 trillion rupiah ($159 million) for the bank's net profit, or some 41 percent higher than the previous year's figure.    \par \par \uc2 MARKET LEVELS    \par \par \uc2 The Jakarta Composite Index ended 0.39 percent higher at 769.793 points on Wednesday.    \par \par \uc2 In New York, markets ended higher with the Dow Jones Industrial Average jumping 1.17 percent to 10,737.7 points and the Nasdaq Composite edged up 0.69 percent to 2,089.66 points.    \par \par \uc2 The rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was being quoted at 8,402/8,407 to the dollar, stronger than late Wednesday's value.     \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040212e02c000jm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
