\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Indonesia c.bank cuts rph overnight rate by 25 bps.   \b0\par\par\uc2 157 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Februar 2004\par 02:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Feb 12 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cut its rupiah overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, also known as FASBI, to 7.50 percent from 7.75 percent with immediate effect, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 Under the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rule the new rate would be applicable to the morning session while the afternoon session rate would be 3.75 percent from 3.875 percent previously.   \par \par \uc2 The cut came after a steeper-than-expected decrease in the interest rate on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's one-month certificate (SBI), which fell by 11 basis points to 7.66 percent on Wednesday, amid expectations of a decline in the FASBI rate.   \par \par \uc2 Some money market dealers had expected Bank Indonesia to cut the overnight rate by 25 basis points, amid benign inflation, a steady rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a lot of extra cash in the money market.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040212e02c0006h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
