\par\par \b \uc2 Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mostly Down Late; Peso At 2-Mo Low  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Ditas Lopez  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 745 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Oktober 2003\par 12:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 MANILA (Dow Jones)--The Philippine peso ended at a two-month low on continued security and political concerns Friday, while other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were also mostly weaker against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Short-dollar covering following a recent sell-off, and importer demand drove dealings across the region, but trading was muted by holidays in Asia, including Singapore and Malaysia.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at 55.330 pesos, its highest level since closing at PHP55.450 on Aug. 26, and was up from PHP55.240 Thursday. Volume declined to $145.2 million from $236.5 million Thursday.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy governor Amando Tetangco said the dollar's recent rally is partly due to corporate demand, particularly from firms covering their month-end debt payments and import requirements.  \par \par \uc2 "The political noise isn't helping. It has been a cautious market," said Tetangco, who noted that banks were also buying dollars ahead of the May 2004 presidential elections. There are concerns of political and security instability in the months leading to the polls.  \par \par \uc2 There have been renewed security concerns following reports that 30 members of the terror Jemaah Islamiyah group remain in the country.  \par \par \uc2 Senior Philippine officials have been trying to calm the markets, and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rafael Buenaventura added his voice Friday, saying the peso should recover from its recent weakness toward the year end when remittances from overseas Filipino workers during Christmas should help support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 He also warned that "we are closely watching the market. If we need to go in, we will, but so far there's no need to do that."  \par \par \uc2 However, traders believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could still sell dollars. "It all depends on how you define \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a Manila trader. "There's nothing that stops the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  from influencing the exchange rate," he added.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Said Didn't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  To Help Rupiah \par    \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also said Friday it won't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the rupiah, which has weakened due mainly to dollar demand from corporates for month-end debt repayments.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The rupiah still trades within a fair range," Anwar Nasution, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  deputy governor, told reporters.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar ended at 8,490 rupiah, higher than IDR8,475 Thursday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Apart from growing demand from local corporates, recent losses in the local equity market also pressured the rupiah.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Some foreign investors sold shares and bought dollars," said a Jakarta trader.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Korean won, meanwhile, fell over the day with market participants suspecting the government hand in the decline, weakening the won to boost exports and support the flagging economy.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But South Korean Minister of Finance and Economy Kim Jin-Pyo stressed Friday that government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market have been aimed only at preventing speculation.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The market shrugged off Kim Jin-Pyo's comments Friday, noting they were somewhat contradictory to earlier remarks that the government will continue to sell won as needed to prevent undue gains, traders said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar climbed to 1,186.8 won before settling at KRW1,185.7 won, preferring to track the gains in non-deliverable forwards and its advance against the yen. The U.S. unit closed at KRW1,184.4 Thursday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Elsewhere, the New Taiwan dollar was weaker on importers' requirements, with interbank players mostly quiet, keeping trades relatively light. The U.S. dollar closed at NT$34.020, up from NT$33.975 a day earlier.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bucking the regional trend was the Thai baht, which gained some ground Friday after a local holiday Thursday. The dollar was trading at 39.815 baht against Wednesday's close of THB39.97. Dollar demand from importers though limited the local unit's gains.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Thailand Friday said that recent limits imposed on outstanding balances of nonresident accounts with local financial institutions to curb speculation in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market had been effective.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar has hovered around THB40 in recent days, recovering from a 40-month low of THB38.95 early October on account of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's measures.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Singapore dollar also strengthened in offshore trading, with onshore markets closed for a public holiday. The U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7414 in late Asian trading, compared with S$1.7418 a day earlier.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Ditas Lopez, Dow Jones Newswires; 632-885-0288; ditas.lopez@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Lim Mui Khi  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1136 4250  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031024dzao000gb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
