\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesian Rupiah Ends Higher With Region, S&P Upgrade  \b0\par\par\uc2 367 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2003\par 11:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah ended stronger Wednesday in line with other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and after Standard & Poor's upgraded the country's sovereign rating by one notch.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended Asian trading at 8,365 rupiah, down from IDR8,395 at Tuesday's close.  \par \par \uc2 The yen's strength against the dollar lent a positive tone to trading in other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday, and this filtered through to the rupiah, dealers said. Despite heavy dollar buying by Asian central banks, aimed at limiting gains in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , most Asian units ended higher.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the government has said it's happy with a dollar trading range of between IDR8,200 and IDR8,700. If the dollar falls through the support at the lower end of this range, however, they expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell rupiah to maintain the country's export competitiveness.  \par \par \uc2 S&P's move Wednesday to raise Indonesia's foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating to B from B-minus also helped boost the rupiah, traders said. It was the ratings agency's second upgrade for Indonesia this year, and shows growing confidence in the country's ability to continue managing its finances prudently without the International Monetary Fund next year, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expect the U.S. unit to trade between IDR8,300 and IDR8,400 Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Expected capital inflows to purchase state-owned assets are also underpinning the rupiah.  \par \par \uc2 Next week, the government will launch an international roadshow to promote its upcoming initial public offering of a 30% stake in state-owned PT Bank Rakyat Indonesia. Pre-marketing for the issue has shown strong foreign demand for the IPO, the underwriters say.  \par \par \uc2 The Indonesian Bank Restructuring Agency is also planning to sell a majority stake in PT Bank Internasional Indonesia later this year. But IBRA said late Tuesday it was willing to cancel the sale of PT Bank Lippo, which is also on the auction block, because so far no credible bidder had shown interest in the sale.  \par \par \uc2 -By Tom Wright, Dow Jones Newswires; 6221 3983 1277; tom.wright@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 1159 1848  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031008dza8000hu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
