\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  says no rph  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  right now. \b0\par\par\uc2 237 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 August 2003\par 09:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Aug 29 (Reuters) - Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday it would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market right now to prop up the rupiah, under selling pressure over the past few days, saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains largely stable. \par \par \uc2  When asked by reporters whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  right now, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy governor Aslim Tadjuddin said: "There is no need to do so. It is still stable. There is no such need." \par \par \uc2  His comments came as the rupiah  on Friday continued to be pressured by month-end imports and market expectations falling interest rates may erode its attractiveness to investors. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was quoted at around 8,550 against the dollar in afternoon trade on Friday, down from some 8,505 in late trade the previous day. \par \par \uc2  Despite falls in recent days, the rupiah remained among the best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region, gaining some 4.7 percent against the dollar so far this year. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its overnight rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate (FASBI), a key policy tool, by 50 basis points to 8.5 percent on Friday, the seventh time since May. \par \par \uc2  The FASBI has been cut seven times since the beginning of May, reducing the rate by a total of 275 basis poi