\par\par \b \uc2  Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  Deputy Gov: To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  To Guard Rupiah \b0\par\par\uc2 221 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 2003\par 04:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Wednesday it will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rupiah after a bomb killed at least 14 people in a downtown Jakarta hotel. \par \par \uc2  The bomb blast Tuesday sent the rupiah and stocks tumbling on fears that Islamic militant groups are stepping up attacks on President Megawati Sukarnoputri's government. \par \par \uc2  "Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is committed to defend the rupiah. We will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if necessary," Aslim Tajudin, a deputy governor, told Dow Jones Newswires. He added the rupiah should recover soon. \par \par \uc2  At 0220 GMT, the dollar was at 8,665 rupiah, up from IDR8,480 before the bomb. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia has foreign reserves of more than $33 billion, meaning it can easily move the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which isn't widely traded by foreign investors. \par \par \uc2  But the rupiah is likely to remain under pressure in the short term as players fear further terrorist attacks ahead of the verdict in the trial of a key suspect in last year's Bali bombing, which killed more than 200 mainly Western tourists. The court will hand down its verdict Thursday on Amrozi bin Nurhasyim, a ringleader of the attack who faces the death penalty. \par \par \uc2  -By I Made Sentana, Dow Jones newswires; 6221 3983 1277; i-made.sentana@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  -Edited by Mary de Wet \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030806dz860003i\par }\page {\pa