\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupiah, Sing hit by blast - Seoul buys won. \b0\par\par\uc2 735 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 2003\par 11:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Aug 5 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah fell\par nearly two percent on Tuesday to a one-week low, rocked by the\par bombing of the Marriott Hotel in central Jakarta, which also\par triggered knee-jerk selling of the Singapore dollar.\par  \par     Meanwhile, U.S. dollar purchases by authorities in South\par Korean pulled the won to a one-month low.\par     The rupiah slipped to 8,650 per dollar, from late Monday's\par 8,490, in response to the blast which killed six people and\par wounded dozens.\par     Dealers said initial response was muted as the incident\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  happened during the local market's lunch break. Later, local \par \par \uc2  brokers quoted the rupiah in a wide 8,560/8670 range, \par \par \uc2  indicating few people were willing to trade. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a foreign bank in Jakarta said most players \par \par \uc2  were still reluctant to aggressively sell the rupiah fearing \par \par \uc2  that might provoke an aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  response. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "There was some speculation of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bids so the\par market is very cautious," one dealer said.\par     The rupiah had hit a three-month low of 8,725 last month,\par as mainly foreign players unwound long rupiah carry trades.\par That provoked heavy \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Bhanu Baweja, UBS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist in Singapore, said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the risks of investing in Indonesia were well known, and so\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par markets were not likely to be too unsettled for an extended\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par period.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "Most of the people who are in Indonesia really do know the\par security risk that goes along with investing in this place."\par     The rupiah's fall accentuated losses in the Singapore\par dollar , and pulled it to a three-month low of 1.7661 per\par dollar.\par     It was quickly pushed back to levels on the stronger side\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of the technically crucial 1.7650, a level the market had\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par breached but failed to close above on June 30, July 18 and last\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The downside was limited by data showing an expansion in\par the manufacturing sector for the second straight month in July.\par     WON HITS 1-MONTH LOWS\par     The South Korean won                  was sold down to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1,189.0 per U.S. dollar, its weakest since July 2, after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dealers said they spotted dollar purchases from the finance\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ministry apparently aimed at soaking up equity-related dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par James Malcolm, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at JP Morgan Chase in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore, said South Korean authorities had been buying\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars since Friday and that given the yen's weakness on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tuesday those purchases might have picked up.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Despite the won's losses, it stayed on the strong side of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 10 on the yen-won cross , where it has been since\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par mid-July.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We are still in an environment where central banks in Asia\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par are reluctant to see their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciate," Malcolm\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     An over three percent rise in Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par reserves to $182 billion backed those views.\par     Dealers in Singapore said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has absorbed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par most foreign inflows to keep the Taiwan dollar  locked\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in a narrow 34.30-34.50 per U.S. dollar range since it hit a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 10-month high of 34.25 in July.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippine peso  kept in sight of Monday's local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close of 54.80, amid speculation the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has raised\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its monitoring of dollar purchases by banks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The peso fell to four-month lows just shy of the 55 per\par dollar level last week after a failed mutiny on July 27.\par     The Thai baht       , tracking moves in the region, eased\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to the weaker side of the 42 per dollar level. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. DOLLAR AT 0855 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     120.44       119.88         -0.46\par  Sing dlr      1.7655       1.7590         -0.37\par  Taiwan dlr    34.466       34.430         -0.10\par  Korean won   1187.90      1