\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian stocks, rupiah dive after Jakarta blast. \b0\par\par\uc2 494 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 2003\par 10:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Aug 5 (Reuters) - Indonesian share prices and the rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  plunged on Tuesday after a huge explosion in a luxury hotel in Jakarta's business district that killed at least eight people. \par \par \uc2  The main stock market index fell almost five percent to its lowest since May 27 after the explosion in the basement of the Marriott Hotel reinforced worries about the law and order situation in the world's most populous Muslim nation. The market later recovered some of the losses. \par \par \uc2  No one has claimed responsibility for the blast, which wounded at least 83 people seriously. \par \par \uc2  "Stocks fell because of the explosion. I heard it is very damaging. It raises fresh concerns over the security condition," said a local dealer. \par \par \uc2  At 0800 GMT, the index was down 2.74 percent. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah also weakened, with quotes down around two percent on the day to 8,670 per dollar - although the fall was limited by the likelihood of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Major banks are not moving as they fear the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may soon come in," one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer in Jakarta said. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah avoided a three month low of 8,725 per dollar hit in late July, and still remains the strongest Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the U.S. dollar this year. \par \par \uc2  The blast coincided with high-profile trials in Indonesia of suspected Islamic militants on bomb-related charges - including influential Muslim cleric Abu Bakar Bashir, accused of leading the Jemmah Islamiah group which has been blamed for a series of attacks on Western targets in the country. \par \par \uc2  A court in Bali was expected to deliver its first verdict on Thursday in the trials of those charged with planting a bomb that killed over 200 people on the resort island in October last year. \par \par \uc2  Bhanu Baweja, UBS \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist in Singapore, said the risks of investing in Indonesia were well known, and so markets were not likely to be too unsettled for an extended period. \par \par \uc2  "Most of the people who are in Indonesia really do know the security risk that goes along with investing in this place," he said. \par \par \uc2  "I think security risk is probably on the rise slightly, but you haven't seen the international investor come into Indonesia in a very big way in any case." \par \par \uc2  When the rupiah slumped in July as investors switched out of Indonesia's high-yielding debt and into equity markets elsewhere, the losses were stemmed by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Last week, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Burhanuddin Abdullah told Reuters he expected the rupiah to trade between 8,200 and 8,600 per dollar for the rest of the year. \par \par \uc2  Asked about the amount of foreign funds flowing into Indonesia, he said: "In the past two months around $4 billion came in - around $2 billion in the form of FDI, around $1 billion into the stock market or portfolio investment and $1 billion in the money market, i.e. hot money." \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030805dz8500gu4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
