\par\par \b \uc2  CORRECTED - CORRECTED-Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Mutiny knocks peso, others firm. \b0\par\par\uc2 733 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juli 2003\par 08:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     In SINGAPORE story headlined "Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -Mutiny\par knocks peso, others firm", please read in second paragraph\par ...having closed at 54.01 on Friday... instead of ...having\par closed at 54.01 on Monday. (Corrects day.)\par     A corrected story follows.\par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, July 28 (Reuters) - The Philippine peso\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  dropped by more than a percent to four-month lows early on \par \par \uc2  Monday as investors sold the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a failed weekend \par \par \uc2  mutiny by soldiers in Manila. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The peso touched 54.60 per dollar minutes after the open of\par local trade, having closed at 54.01 on Friday.\par     It pared its losses to around 54.25, a move dealers said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was prompted by the fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par further weakness was expected as investors reassessed their\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exposures.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "People would want to see where \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  draws the line\par in the sand," said a dealer at a local bank in Manila.\par     Rovic De Guzman, head of trading at the Union Bank of the\par Philippines in Manila, said the 54.60 level might hold for some\par time, but the future direction for peso was down.\par     "There was no bloodshed in the incident so it will help,\par but the fact that it happened will have its impact on\par investors."\par     On the weekend, hundreds of soldiers took over and wired a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par premier shopping and apartment complex in Manila with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par explosives, accusing the government of corruption and collusion\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with Muslim rebels. They surrendered on Sunday after hours of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par negotiations.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said people were waiting to see what President\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Gloria Macapagal Arroyo had to say in an address to the nation\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par due later in the afternoon.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Rating agency Standard & Poor's said on Monday it was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sticking to its BB-rating and stable outlook for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Philippines.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Judging by the public information the political issues are\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par relatively minor in the medium to long-term," Takahira Ogawa,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par S&P's director for Asia-Pacific sovereign ratings, told\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reuters.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par YEN HELPS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Elsewhere, a steadier yen  and month-end settlement\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of export deals helped other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  retain a firm\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bias.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar  rose to 1.7460 per U.S. dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ahead of June manufacturing data at 0500 GMT. The data is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected to show a pick-up from May when SARS hit ouput.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai baht  rose to 41.88 per dollar, from late\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Friday's 41.96, with dollar sales by exporters adding distance\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to one-month lows on the weaker side of 42 hit last week after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  relaxed some \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  controls.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Indonesian rupiah  was also recovering from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par three-month lows it had hit last week, mainly prompted by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par unwinding of carry trades.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The rupiah rose to around 8,490 per dollar, from Thursday's\par three-month low of 8,725.\par     Dealers said recent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to place\par a floor under the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has prompted players to trim long\par dollar positions, although market sentiment was still fragile.\par     "We still target (dollar/rupiah) to rise to 9,000 handle by\par end of third quarter," said James Malcolm, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist\par at JP Morgan Chase in Singapore.\par     The South Korean won                   rose to 1,178.8 per\par dollar on month-end exporters' dollar sales and inflow of\par foreign investment in local equities.\par     The Taiwan dollar          rose to 34.33 per U.S. dollar,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par where it also peaked on Thursday and Friday, as local stocks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   hitting a year high in early trade, before falling back\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to around 34.40. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0238 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     119.13       118.99      