\par\par \b \uc2  PRESS DIGEST-Indonesian Business News - July 24. \b0\par\par\uc2 326 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juli 2003\par 03:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  Following are the leading business stories in the main Indonesian newspapers on July 24. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy. \par \par \uc2  Telephone: Editorial, (6221) 384-6364. Fax (6221) 344-8404 or Help Desk, (6221) 344-8406. Fax: (6221) 381-0862 \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  KOMPAS \par \par \uc2  - BANK \b \highlight22\uc2 INDONESIA INTERVENES\b0 \highlight\uc2  TO HELP THE RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since Tuesday to stem the fall of the rupiah , governor Burhanuddin Abdullah said. \par \par \uc2  - BUMI SAYS DIVESTMENT OF KPC WILL CONTINUE \par \par \uc2  Exploration firm PT Bumi Resources (BUMI.JK), which recently bought BP Plc (BP.L) and Rio Tinto's (RIO.L) stakes in PT Kaltim Prima Coal (KPC) for $500 million, said it would stick to a government ruling and divest a 51 percent stake in the coal miner. \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  THE JAKARTA POST \par \par \uc2  - RUPIAH FALLS TO THREE-MONTH LOW \par \par \uc2  The rupiah fell to its lowest level in three months on Wednesday as foreign investors continued buying dollars after selling rupiah-denominated assets. \par \par \uc2  - LOCAL GOVERNMENT MAY HALT \b \highlight22\uc2 OPERATIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2  AT KPC \par \par \uc2  The East Kalimantan provincial administration threatened on Wednesday to stop the \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  of coal mining firm KPC following what it said was a surprise decision by Rio Tinto and BP to sell full ownership of the company to Bumi Resources. \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  EKONOMI NERACA \par \par \uc2  - PERTAMINA TO INCREASE GAS PRICES NEXT MONTH \par \par \uc2  State oil and gas firm Pertamina will increase the price of liquefied petroleum gas by around five percent and gas fuel by around 50 percent starting next month in a bid to reach a break even point. But it will reduce the price of gas tube by around 25 percent. \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  BISNIS INDONESIA \par \par \uc2  - SBI FALLS FOUR BASIS POINTS TO 9.17 PERCENT \par \par \uc2  The interest rate on Indonesia's one-month \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  paper (SBI) fell four basis points to 9.17 percent on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  Looking for more information from local sources? For details, please call your local help desk . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030724dz7o002xr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
